Subject: [PATCH 54/54] feat(admin): an old-profile fixture for 4226, fictional
 contacts only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 49805: 4226 (the owner's corrected job wins over a contact's
old Ally profile) cannot be tested — no chat can give a fictional contact
an old profile.

POST /admin/test-accounts/:id/fixtures/old-profile
  { phone, employer, job_position }
writes employer and "jobPosition" on the account that holds that number.
Both sides must be fictional: the seat must be a test seat, the number one
of its own contacts, and the account behind the number a test seat as well.
A real person's profile is never matched, and the UPDATE itself re-checks
test_seats. 400 for an empty profile, 403 when either side is not a test
seat, 404 when the number is not the seat's contact.

DONE WHEN: the tester sets an old profile on a fictional contact and runs
4226's two cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
